      "disclaimers": [
        {
          "t": 1300.6,
          "kind": "other",
          "text": "there is a dedicated uh session uh recorded in this launch event uh that covers datadriven testing in depth"
        },
        {
          "t": 1587,
          "kind": "other",
          "text": "And again, we're going to have a full session on this."
        }
      ],
      "quotes": [
        {
          "t": 265.5,
          "text": "You don't have to download the symbols. You don't have to create the dependent species before you can actually find the symbols."
        },
        {
          "t": 479.8,
          "text": "This is critical for allowing you to extend the interfaces over time."
        },
        {
          "t": 564.3,
          "text": "So now with the default implementation we can extend an interface and build our solution across many releases without breaking any of our consumers."
        },
        {
          "t": 619,
          "text": "they're actually merged into uh the the base uh table and that means that a key can now span uh both base and extension fields at the same time"
        },
        {
          "t": 694.4,
          "text": "The public resources are actually consumable without a dependency."
        },
        {
          "t": 775.4,
          "text": "if you try to get a private resource by and providing the app ID, you will get an error."
        },
        {
          "t": 787.3,
          "text": "So be mindful about taking hard dependencies on specific apps on public resources because if they stop shipping it,"
        },
        {
          "t": 820.2,
          "text": "that sometimes the ledger entries or some of the other the sequence entries run out of numbers."
        },
        {
          "t": 833.4,
          "text": "So we made it possible for you to switch to big integer by changing the type."
        },
        {
          "t": 872.7,
          "text": "Just changing the type itself does not change all the places where you use this value."
        },
        {
          "t": 919.7,
          "text": "but it's still allowed and it will still pass through and you can actually do this change without having to copy data"
        },
        {
          "t": 1045.1,
          "text": "This will now generate XL files with a fully qualified name as the ids."
        },
        {
          "t": 1173.9,
          "text": "These are not fields that I have created. They're part of the system fields on the record now."
        },
        {
          "t": 1289.6,
          "text": "run the whole suite from the command line and get structured JSON with pass fail and skip counts plus a real exit code"
        },
        {
          "t": 1392.9,
          "text": "So for every single entry that exists in this data set, this platform will execute this test and provide the result for it."
        },
        {
          "t": 1529.8,
          "text": "So I have the flexibility of handling things outside the test case in a common way both globally but also specifically for a specific test code unit."
        },
        {
          "t": 1654.6,
          "text": "Counter to the LSP which is actually looking at the project as it is now."
        },
        {
          "t": 1666.7,
          "text": "This is a static thing that we can do offline as long as we extract uh the information that we need to query on beforehand."
        },
        {
          "t": 1848.2,
          "text": "coding agents can now capture the performance profiles and the snapshot recordings themselves through dedicated MCP uh tools with no active debugging session"
        },
        {
          "t": 1861.9,
          "text": "You still need to judge uh what the evidence that it find means"
        },
        {
          "t": 2007.1,
          "text": "Why are these called proxies? This is because the actual work all happens on the server."
        },
        {
          "t": 2018.2,
          "text": "There's no snapshot or um performance profiling being done on the client side. It's all being done on the server side."
        },
        {
          "t": 2034.7,
          "text": "this release has been around making agents more capable making it easier for agents to work with the code"
        },
        {
          "t": 2070.9,
          "text": "You don't need to adopt everything at once. Start with a gap that you have today"
        }
      ],
